# The dated Debian archive every hosted guest job installs from. `sid` is a
# rolling release and its QEMU is the instrument this project's numbers are
# taken on: on 2026-08-31 it moved 11.1.0 to 11.1.1 mid-afternoon and every
# guest job refused at `instrument.sh`, correctly, because a number taken on
# one QEMU is not a number about the other. Installing from a snapshot makes
# the instrument a decision rather than a delivery date.
#
# This date and `.github/qemu-version` are one fact in two files: the date is
# one on which `sid` carried that QEMU. Moving either alone is a mistake, and
# `src/ci.rs` holds every workflow's copy of this string against this file.
20260831T000000Z
